{
  "spec": "hitch/1",
  "description": "Initial catalogue. floor is the minimum answer tier (a mod may raise it, never lower it). safety != none: no grants, no default, no fallback. privacy is the node-set class for the type's data. kinds marked decision:true are decision kinds. verbFloors lowers the floor for named verbs that run no side effect (default {decline: narrow}); it never names the verb that executes. Vendor kinds not listed default to floor local until a local decision assigns one. reachesOut: when a decision of that kind reaches another machine (request flag reachesOut), floor and safety are raised to these values (Tyler, 2026-11-24: a parley send that leaves the machine is always a safety send). vendorPending: the owner (not this project) writes the schema; catalog-check reports it as a warning that does not fail the gate unless --strict. declaredOnly: declared but not emitted yet (reason given); the whole-catalogue audit warns, and emitting it without a schema fails the --emitted gate as usual. item: an item kind (hitch.item@1 resources), checked by --emitted like any type. transitional: removed at that phase. personOps: the person-only operations a paired client may call directly (POST /hitch/v1/person/:op), each with its tier, body schema, secret fields and the decision kinds it may close (closes). An op with secret fields must be tier local. testOnly ops never ship.",
